    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26921" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏgēum</span></b> , i, and
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŏgĭum</span></b> ,
			ĭi, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λογεῖον</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγιον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that part of
				the stage on which the actors spoke, the pulpitum</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5, 8,
				3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Archives</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quoniam de logeo parum provisum est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 5, 20, 6</span></i>
			 dub.</div>
